Subject: Align SAVED_VAR.desired_setting as void* for Fil-C pointer capabilities
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: Bash unwind_prot stores saved pointer variables inside SAVED_VAR.desired_setting; using void*[1] instead of char[1] preserves Fil-C pointer alignment and capability metadata.
Upstream-Status: Upstreamable
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: 15d13b236893

--- a/unwind_prot.c
+++ b/unwind_prot.c
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 typedef struct {
   char *variable;
   int size;
-  char desired_setting[1]; /* actual size is `size' */
+  void *desired_setting[1]; /* actual size is `size' */
 } SAVED_VAR;
 
 /* If HEAD.CLEANUP is null, then ARG.V contains a tag to throw back to.
